Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a Topology Response without Associated Clients empties the BSSs it lists

A Topology Response's Associated Clients TLV is the controller's repair for a client leave it
missed: handle_topology_response_clients takes it as the agent's whole association snapshot and
removes the associations it omits. EasyMesh includes that TLV only when a client is associated
with one of the agent's BSSs, so an agent whose BSSs have emptied sends none, and a leave the
controller missed on such a BSS stayed in its model (STAList Associated) across every later
response and cold start.

A response with an AP Operational BSS TLV and no Associated Clients TLV now empties the BSSs that
TLV lists: each station still associated on one of them, in every model of the sender's agent,
leaves as a Topology Notification's leave does (remove_sta_assoc, the notification's leave branch
moved into a helper both use: an MLD's affiliated links marked unassociated, else the station's
own row removed and kept as a disassociation row, then the association event with assoc_event 0).
A BSS the response does not list keeps its stations; a malformed AP Operational BSS TLV changes
nothing. Each such response that removed stations is logged with the agent's counts since start:
its removals, and its responses without the TLV (every one, removals or not). An agent that omits
the TLV with clients associated, whose stations would then leave at each response and come back
with its next notifications, shows as removals in nearly every response. A response with the TLV
is reconciled as before.

The frame routing's drop of a frame for a BSS the sender's model lacks ("Could not find bss") was
a debug line: a client's join or leave lost there left no trace. It is now logged per message type
and sender, the first at once and then at most one line a minute with the count since: an ERROR
for a Topology Notification (it carries a client's join or leave), INFO for the other types
(metrics, capability and BTM reports, which drop while an agent onboards). Only senders with a
model reach the drop, for five message types, but the pairs kept are capped all the same at 256:
pairs quiet for 10 minutes go first, and while none is, new pairs' drops are counted together
under one overflow entry, logged as an ERROR at most once a minute.

Tests: a_leave_without_an_mld_removes_the_live_owner (the shared leave path);
operational_bssids_lists_every_bss_of_every_radio and operational_bssids_refuses_a_malformed_tlv
(the TLV's walk, a radio with no BSS, a cut SSID, a trailing byte);
listed_associations_takes_associated_stations_on_listed_bsss_only (an unlisted BSS keeps its
station, an unassociated row is no leave); the_first_is_logged_then_one_line_a_minute_with_the_count
and the_pairs_are_capped_and_the_rest_counted_together (the routing drop's line, the cap, the
overflow entry and its count, quiet pairs going first).
